Skip a shuffle swap of a cell, column, or row with itself.

The data shuffling tool pairs cells (columns, rows) at random and swaps
each pair through a temporary area with three sheet_move_range calls.
When a pair is one and the same, the second move has no offset and
sheet_move_range refuses it with a CRITICAL assertion (origin_sheet !=
target_sheet || col_offset != 0 || row_offset != 0); the cells end up
right, but every shuffle of a small range logs the assertion, twice for
the undo.  Found through the Cocoa front end on 2026-10-12; the GTK
front end runs the same code.  Return before the moves when there is
nothing to swap.

--- a/src/tools/data-shuffling.c	2026-10-12 20:31:03
+++ b/src/tools/data-shuffling.c	2026-10-12 20:31:03
@@ -145,6 +145,9 @@
 {
         GnmExprRelocateInfo reverse;
 
+	if (sw->a.col == sw->b.col && sw->a.row == sw->b.row)
+		return;
+
 	reverse.reloc_type = GNM_EXPR_RELOCATE_MOVE_RANGE;
         reverse.target_sheet = st->sheet;
         reverse.origin_sheet = st->sheet;
@@ -179,6 +182,9 @@
 {
         GnmExprRelocateInfo reverse;
 
+	if (sw->a.col == sw->b.col)
+		return;
+
 	reverse.reloc_type = GNM_EXPR_RELOCATE_MOVE_RANGE;
         reverse.target_sheet = st->sheet;
         reverse.origin_sheet = st->sheet;
@@ -213,6 +219,9 @@
 {
         GnmExprRelocateInfo reverse;
 
+	if (sw->a.row == sw->b.row)
+		return;
+
 	reverse.reloc_type = GNM_EXPR_RELOCATE_MOVE_RANGE;
         reverse.target_sheet = st->sheet;
         reverse.origin_sheet = st->sheet;
